1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,679
I just got back from a trip to texas and I have to say that as a french person I have a lot of thoughts.
我刚从得州旅行回来。作为一个法国人，我有很多想法。

2
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:13,040
So texas is one of the most well known and most stereotyped states of the us and that's exactly why I wanted to see it for myself.
得州在美国各州中既很有名，也常被贴上刻板印象，所以我特别想亲自去看看。

3
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:16,320
So today I want to share a few observations from my trip with you.
今天我想和你们分享旅途中的一些观察。

4
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:23,119
So so far I've been to quite a few places around texas and my first impression is that it's both massive and super diverse.
目前我已经去过得州不少地方，第一印象是它既庞大又非常多样。

5
00:00:23,119 --> 00:00:29,519
Like for example in terms of size texas is a bit bigger than france and there's roughly half of the population.
比如按她的比较，得州面积比法国略大，人口大约只有一半。

6
00:00:29,519 --> 00:00:32,479
And depending on where you go things can be very different.
而且去的地方不同，情况会很不一样。

7
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:38,159
Like for example there was a fully different vibes first between cities and the countryside but also between cities themselves.
比如城市和乡村的氛围完全不同，城市彼此之间也有差异；原字幕 fully different vibes 待听辨。

8
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:43,840
Like it seems very different to live in austin versus san antonio or the dallas fort worth area.
住在奥斯汀、圣安东尼奥，或达拉斯—沃思堡一带，感觉似乎很不一样。

9
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:49,830
We're going to get into specifics later but obviously with texas being so big there's not one single texas experience.
稍后会讲具体细节。不过得州这么大，显然不存在唯一一种“得州体验”。

10
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,080
So please share how things are where you live with me.
所以，请分享你所在地方的情况。

11
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:56,240
And even though I feel I've done quite a lot in texas I still feel I have so much to discover.
虽然我觉得自己在得州已经做了很多事，但仍有很多东西值得探索。

12
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:02,240
Because each region is pretty different and things are really big so you can end up driving a lot we'll get back to this point in a bit.
每个地区都很不同，地方又大，结果可能要开很多车。这个点稍后再说。

13
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:06,719
But first I want to tell you about my favorite things in texas starting with the people.
先说我在得州最喜欢的事情，从人开始。

14
00:01:06,719 --> 00:01:12,640
So if you're from texas just know that you get a reputation for being nice abroad and I found that to be really true.
得州的朋友要知道，你们在海外有友善的名声，而我发现确实如此。

15
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:16,000
Like all the micro interactions I had there were really next level.
我在那里遇到的那些微小互动，都让我觉得格外出色。

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,359
Either when I was in a cab buying something ordering food every time the people I was talking with were very welcoming and always took the time to have a nice interaction with me.
无论坐出租车、买东西还是点餐，每次和我说话的人都很热情，愿意花时间友好交流。

17
00:01:25,359 --> 00:01:30,640
I've talked about it before but small talk is not as much of a thing in france as it is in the us.
我以前说过，在我看来，闲聊在法国不像在美国那样普遍。

18
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:36,399
And even more in texas it really feels that small talk is an art here and people are super curious.
在得州更明显，我觉得这里把闲聊当成一门艺术，大家也很好奇。

19
00:01:36,399 --> 00:01:42,560
Like I remember being at this neighborhood coffee shop and there were a lot of regulars so I think we like really stood out.
我记得去一家社区咖啡馆，那里有很多常客，所以我觉得我们格外显眼。

20
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:47,840
And people kept asking us where we were from and why we found this place and why we were here.
人们不断问我们从哪里来、怎么找到这里、为什么会来。

21
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:51,679
Which really led to cool conversations that really felt authentic to me.
这带来了很棒的谈话，对我来说感觉很真诚。

22
00:01:51,679 --> 00:01:58,399
My other favorite thing in texas has to be the food there is a very big and unique food culture that I really love.
我在得州另一个最喜欢的东西就是食物。我很喜欢这里庞大且独特的饮食文化。

23
00:01:58,399 --> 00:02:04,880
And you know a lot of the things I like are also valued in texas so like craftsmanship you know the way the food is made.
我喜欢的很多东西，在得州也受到重视，比如手艺、制作食物的方式。

24
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:11,519
We've been to a bunch of barbecue places on and off camera and every time it has been so fun watching the pit masters at work.
我们镜头内外都去了不少烤肉店，每次看烤肉师工作都很有趣。

25
00:02:11,519 --> 00:02:16,239
Because you can tell that it takes so much skill to make a good barbecue and that's something I really value.
因为看得出做好烤肉需要很多技术，而这是我很看重的。

26
00:02:16,239 --> 00:02:22,310
Also as someone who comes from the south of france I always enjoy sharing a good meal and having the meal be an event.
我来自法国南部，总喜欢和别人分享一顿好饭，也喜欢让吃饭本身成为一件重要活动。

27
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:25,920
So that's one of the reasons why barbecue culture really resonated with me.
所以这也是烤肉文化让我产生共鸣的原因之一。

28
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:30,000
But you know barbecue is not the only thing another thing I enjoy is the tmex food.
当然不只是烤肉。我还喜欢她所说的 tmex 食物；该原词疑似识别问题，待核。

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,879
Like during this trip I had my first breakfast taco ever I got one with bacon potatoes eggs cheese and reffried beans.
这次我第一次吃早餐塔可，里面有培根、土豆、鸡蛋、奶酪和豆泥；reffried 原词待核。

30
00:02:36,879 --> 00:02:43,200
I also ordered a second taco with avocado and I have to tell you that after that I was full for the whole morning.
我还点了第二个带牛油果的塔可，之后整个上午都很饱。

31
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:49,439
Also being french I really love wine and it was so fun to see that there's a lot of very good local wines in texas.
另外，作为法国人我很爱葡萄酒，发现得州有很多好喝的本地酒很有趣；好喝为个人评价。

32
00:02:49,439 --> 00:02:52,640
We went to this winery and we ordered their tasting flights.
我们去了一家酒庄，点了他们的品酒组合。

33
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:59,280
So it's like four little glasses with four different wines all of them from texas and it was delicious and such a fun discovery.
就是四个小杯，四种不同的酒，全来自得州。很美味，是一次有趣的发现。

34
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:04,149
And overall I'm such a fan of how many texas specific things there are in texas.
总体来说，我很喜欢得州有这么多带着本地特色的东西。

35
00:03:04,159 --> 00:03:10,159
Like you know when I travel somewhere I really want to be immersed in the culture and also try things that I cannot have at home.
旅行时，我希望沉浸在当地文化中，也尝试在家里体验不到的东西。

36
00:03:10,159 --> 00:03:13,760
And that is why I love grocery shopping so much when I'm in a new place.
所以，我到了新地方就特别喜欢逛食品杂货店。

37
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:17,520
And let me tell you the grocery shopping in texas is next level.
我跟你们说，在得州逛食品杂货店真是格外精彩。
